.IX Title "Lucy::Search::Hits 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Search::Hits 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Search::Hits \- Access search results.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 8
\&    my $hits = $searcher\->hits(
\&        query      => $query,
\&        offset     => 0,
\&        num_wanted => 10,
\&    );
\&    while ( my $hit = $hits\->next ) {
\&        print "<p>$hit\->{title} <em>" . $hit\->get_score . "</em></p>\en";
\&    }
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Hits objects are iterators used to access the results of a search.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS next
.IX Subsection "next"
.Vb 1
\&    my $hit_doc = $hits\->next();
.Ve
.PP
Return the HitDoc for the next hit, or undef when the iterator
is exhausted.
.SS total_hits
.IX Subsection "total_hits"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $hits\->total_hits();
.Ve
.PP
Return the total number of documents which matched the Query used to
produce the Hits object.  Note that this is the total number of
matches, not just the number of matches represented by the Hits
iterator.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Search::Hits isa Clownfish::Obj.
